ARROW HOP - PRIVACY POLICY
Last updated: October 29, 2026

This privacy policy explains how the mobile game "Arrow Hop" (package name: com.oguzhan.arrowhop, "the App") handles information. The App is developed by an independent developer ("we", "us").

1. INFORMATION WE COLLECT
We do not collect, store or share any personal information ourselves. The App has no user accounts, no sign-in and no in-app chat.

Game progress (best score, statistics, unlocked arrows, daily challenge results and settings such as sound and vibration) is saved only on your device. It is never sent to us or to any server. Uninstalling the App deletes this data.

2. ADVERTISING (GOOGLE ADMOB)
The App shows ads through Google AdMob, a service of Google LLC. To show and measure ads, AdMob may automatically collect and process information such as:
- your device's advertising ID (Android Advertising ID),
- IP address and approximate location derived from it,
- device and app information (device model, operating system version, app version, language),
- ad interaction data (for example, ad impressions and clicks),
- diagnostic and performance data.

This information is collected and processed by Google according to Google's own privacy policy:
https://policies.google.com/privacy
How Google uses information from apps that use its services:
https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites

3. CONSENT (EEA, UK AND SWITZERLAND)
If you are in the European Economic Area, the United Kingdom or Switzerland, the App asks for your consent through Google's User Messaging Platform before personalized ads are shown. You can choose to allow or refuse personalized ads. If you refuse, you may still see non-personalized ads.

4. YOUR CHOICES
- You can reset your advertising ID or opt out of personalized ads in your Android settings (Settings > Google > Ads, or Settings > Privacy > Ads, depending on your device).
- You can delete all game data stored on your device by clearing the App's data or uninstalling the App.

5. CHILDREN
The App is not directed at children under the age of 13, and we do not knowingly collect personal information from children. If you believe a child has provided personal information through the App, please contact us and we will help remove it.

6. DATA SECURITY
We do not run servers that store your data. Data handled by Google AdMob is transferred using encryption (HTTPS).

7. CHANGES TO THIS POLICY
We may update this privacy policy from time to time. Changes will be posted on this page with a new "Last updated" date.

